TurboFieldfare is a specialized inference engine for Apple Silicon that enables running the 26-billion-parameter Gemma 4 A4B model on systems with as little as 8 GB of RAM. The core architectural innovation is a hybrid memory strategy that decouples static model components from dynamic routing data. Approximately 1.35 GB of shared weights and the FP16 Key-Value (KV) cache remain resident in system memory at all times. In contrast, the remaining expert weights, which constitute the bulk of the model’s size, are stored on the SSD and streamed into Metal-visible buffers only when required by the router.